//! Typed disk persistence.
//!
//! The disk analog of the typed HTTP client: read/write a proto **type** to
//! disk with validation, instead of hand-rolling file I/O + ad-hoc parsing.
//!
//! Two modes share one substrate (atomic file ops, archive rotation, at-rest
//! compression):
//!
//! 1. **UC1 — atomic typed snapshot** ([`snapshot`]): persist one whole typed
//!    message. Write builds a fresh file and renames it over the original, so
//!    there is never an inconsistent state; the displaced active is archived.
//! 2. **UC2 — redo log** ([`redolog`]): an append-only WAL of typed mutations
//!    (NDJSON), deduped to latest-per-key, periodically compacted via
//!    snapshot+roll with build-then-rename crash recovery.
//!
//! Serialization is **always** via the generated `ToJSON`/`FromJSON` helpers
//! (JSON + newline framing); validation on read is **always on** (we own the
//! data we write, so invalid-on-read is a bug).

